### Using Redux DevTools

One of the greatest benefits of Redux Toolkit is its out-of-the-box integration with the Redux DevTools Extension.

1.  Install the [Redux DevTools Extension](https://chrome.google.com/webstore/detail/redux-devtools/lmhkpmjgfsfkpnpplejcbpnzobcpgpcl?hl=en) for your browser (Chrome and Firefox are supported).
2.  Open your browser's developer tools (F12).
3.  Go to the "Redux" tab.

You'll be able to see:
*   Every action dispatched (e.g., `posts/fetchPosts/pending`, `posts/fetchPosts/fulfilled`, `posts/postAdded`, `posts/reactionAdded`).
*   The state before and after each action.
*   "Time travel debugging" (revert to previous states).

This is incredibly powerful for understanding and debugging your application's state flow!

